	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Type `screenshot` to pick a recent screenshot and copy the image to the clipboard.
Type `screenshot-link` to pick a recent screenshot and copy a markdown image link to the clipboard.

Screenshots are read from ~/Documents/screenshots (most recent first, up to 15).

Type `screenshot-gallery` to browse all screenshots fullscreen in a mosaic (grouped by day):
- click / ↵ : copy image   ⌥ : copy markdown link   ⌘ : reveal in Finder
- ⌘O open · space preview · arrow keys navigate · esc close
The gallery is a small Swift app (gallery.swift), compiled to bin/ on first use; thumbnails are cached in ~/Library/Caches/com.marcotten.alfred-get-screenshot.</string>
